  "body": "Found in #9 round 2 (Adaptive on the developed rotary wrap).\n- On the r6.2 stock the app suites use, the real levels (5.7, 5.2) are refused for out-of-cut travel over 1.5x and cut by Offset rings; only the r7-stock fixture exercises Adaptive on real material. The 5.0 level on r7 is refused by the planning budget after 86 revolutions.\n- A 10 mm developed window at stepdown 2 mm: the planner narrowed the helix to 0.9 and then reported an overload.\n- The load margin on the r7 fixture is thin: 19.5 % D measured vs the 19.7 % law.\n\nDone means: the r6.2 levels plan on Adaptive within the travel budget (or the refusal is decided final with readings), the narrowed-helix overload is gone or refused by name before planning, pinned in rotary_adaptive.",
